# `inst.core.run(x)` outside loops; `run` is a function kept in a field of Core, `core` a field of Schema that holds its declared type. The guess on `inst` proves L0 of what `core` holds. The stretch
# ended behind the read of `core` (three tests on the typed way, then `PropGet run` and the call closed behind the meeting). Now the typed way reads `run` out of its slot, the closed arm reads both names,
# and the receiver and the callee meet: behind the meeting stands the call alone. f1 = apply.
# RUN: walk f1 mechanisms=all
# CHECK-LABEL: code f1:Body
# CHECK: = ShapeTest {{*}}layouts=[L1]
# CHECK: frequency=Rare
# CHECK-NEXT: = PropGet {{*}}key="core"
# CHECK-NEXT: = PropGet {{*}}key="run"
# CHECK: = GetSlot {{*}}key="core" receivers=[L1] level=Proven
# CHECK: = IsSlotFilled {{*}}key="run" receivers=[L0] level=Proven
# CHECK: = GetSlot {{*}}key="run" receivers=[L0] level=Proven
# CHECK-NOT: = PropGet
# CHECK: = Call {{*}}calleeKey="run"
# -- source: a-function-kept-in-a-field-of-a-field-is-read-out-of-its-slot-for-its-call-outside-loops.ts
